1
00:00:07,275 --> 00:00:10,812
This is THRIVE, the Teacher Hub for Resources,.

2
00:00:10,272 --> 00:00:14,460
Instruction, Verified Information and Empowerment.

3
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:19,325
It is built for teachers working in India's government and low-fee schools,.

4
00:00:18,772 --> 00:00:23,485
Where one teacher often handles several grade groups at once.

5
00:00:23,535 --> 00:00:26,562
THRIVE is built around that reality.

6
00:00:26,863 --> 00:00:32,411
When a teacher signs in, everything needed for the day sits on one calm page.

7
00:00:32,461 --> 00:00:38,701
Saved plans, training progress, and the latest updates from the education department,.

8
00:00:38,261 --> 00:00:41,300
Each linked back to an official source.

9
00:00:41,601 --> 00:00:45,886
The heart of THRIVE is the Multi-Grade Classroom Compiler.

10
00:00:45,936 --> 00:00:49,226
A teacher says which grades are in the room,.

11
00:00:48,686 --> 00:00:52,336
For how long, and what the children should learn.

12
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:55,436
THRIVE builds one coordinated period.

13
00:00:55,486 --> 00:00:59,963
A shared opening, a dedicated teacher-led turn for each grade,.

14
00:00:59,436 --> 00:01:05,474
Independent work for the groups who are waiting, and the minutes always add up exactly.

15
00:01:05,523 --> 00:01:09,451
And if the plan is not possible in the time available,.

16
00:01:08,886 --> 00:01:13,564
THRIVE says so, and explains why, instead of hiding it.

17
00:01:13,863 --> 00:01:17,150
When a teacher is not sure where to start,.

18
00:01:16,660 --> 00:01:21,561
Guided setup asks a few simple questions and prepares the plan.

19
00:01:21,611 --> 00:01:27,376
Any part of it can be changed, and every section can be regenerated on its own,.

20
00:01:26,823 --> 00:01:30,263
So a teacher's own edits are never lost.

21
00:01:30,563 --> 00:01:33,386
Then there is the Teaching Assistant.

22
00:01:33,436 --> 00:01:36,925
A teacher can ask, in English or in Hindi,.

23
00:01:36,410 --> 00:01:41,335
How to explain evaporation using nothing but chalk and a blackboard.

24
00:01:41,386 --> 00:01:45,251
The answer is built from THRIVE's curriculum corpus,.

25
00:01:44,686 --> 00:01:49,285
And every reply shows its sources, so it can be checked.

26
00:01:49,335 --> 00:01:55,288
When the corpus does not cover something, THRIVE says so, rather than making it up.

27
00:01:55,588 --> 00:02:00,423
The Training Centre holds short practice modules written by THRIVE.

28
00:02:00,473 --> 00:02:02,351
Progress is saved,.

29
00:02:01,811 --> 00:02:07,711
And each module links to verified professional development from DIKSHA and NISHTHA.

30
00:02:07,761 --> 00:02:11,713
It is a learning record, not an official certificate.

31
00:02:12,013 --> 00:02:17,463
Verified Education Updates collects policy news and official resources,.

32
00:02:17,023 --> 00:02:20,711
Each with its source, with search and bookmarks.

33
00:02:20,761 --> 00:02:25,513
No unverified circulars, and no invented announcements.

34
00:02:25,813 --> 00:02:31,376
And the Teacher Community lets teachers share what actually works in the classroom,.

35
00:02:30,836 --> 00:02:34,713
With replies, helpful votes, and moderation.

36
00:02:46,613 --> 00:02:49,576
THRIVE. Helping teachers thrive, so students flourish.
